<h3 id="what-changes">What changes for you</h3>
<p>Your products move to Gumroad, and buyers check out on Gumroad instead of on ArtStation. Gumroad processes each new sale and pays you for it. Each sale belongs to one place: an order placed on ArtStation before the move stays with ArtStation.</p>

<h3 id="the-link">Open the link ArtStation sends you</h3>
<p>When your products are ready to move, ArtStation emails you a one-time link. Nothing moves until you open the link and confirm.</p>
<ul>
  <li>If you already have a Gumroad account, sign in to it. Use the account with the email address that ArtStation has for you, so that your products go to the right account.</li>
  <li>If you do not have a Gumroad account, the page creates one. We then email you a link to set a password and accept the terms.</li>
</ul>
<p>The link works only once. If it has expired, ask ArtStation for a new one.</p>

<h3 id="getting-paid">Set your payout method</h3>
<p>Gumroad pays you for your sales on Gumroad. The bank account on your ArtStation account does not move to Gumroad, so add a payout method in <a href="https://gumroad.com/settings/payments">Payments settings</a>. You cannot publish a product until you save a payout method.</p>
<p>By default, payouts go out weekly when your balance is $100 USD or more, and a sale waits 7 days before it can be paid out. <a href="13-getting-paid">Getting paid</a> has the full schedule, the payout day for your country, and the fees.</p>

<h3 id="india">If ArtStation paid you to a bank in India</h3>
<p>Gumroad cannot set up new bank payouts to Indian bank accounts. If you already get Gumroad payouts to an Indian bank account, nothing changes. If you do not, use PayPal:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Go to <a href="https://gumroad.com/settings/payments">Payments settings</a>.</li>
  <li>Choose <b>PayPal</b>.</li>
  <li>Enter the email address of your PayPal account. A free Personal account works, but it must be in your own name.</li>
  <li>Click <b>Update settings</b> at the top of the page.</li>
</ol>

<h3 id="drafts">Check and publish your products</h3>
<p>Each product arrives as a draft with its files, cover, and price. Each license option becomes a version of the product. Gumroad does not publish anything for you, and buyers cannot buy a draft.</p>
<p>For each draft:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Open the draft and check the files, the price, and the cover.</li>
  <li>Fix anything that did not move the way you want. For example, replace a file that you changed on ArtStation after you confirmed the move.</li>
  <li>Publish the product. It then appears on your Gumroad profile, with a Gumroad link that you can share.</li>
</ol>

<h3 id="stays">What stays with ArtStation</h3>
<p>Orders placed on ArtStation before the move stay with ArtStation. This includes refunds, chargebacks, tax, and buyer support for those orders. ArtStation supports those buyers for 60 days after its checkout closes. If a past buyer contacts you about an ArtStation order, send them to ArtStation support.</p>
<p>Your past buyers and their orders do not move to Gumroad, so your ArtStation sales do not appear in your Gumroad account.</p>

<h3 id="help">If something looks wrong</h3>
<p>If a product has a missing file, a wrong price, or a wrong version, fix it on the draft. You can also edit the product after you publish it.</p>
<p>If a whole product is missing, or the link does not work, email <a href="mailto:support@gumroad.com">support@gumroad.com</a>. Include the email address on your Gumroad account and the product name, and we will check the move for you.</p>
